2026-09-11 04:42:13 - Received stdin data: {"session_id":"3b215427-ef27-4ece-9d6c-d090047e71d4","transcript_path":"/tmp/.claude/projects/-tmp-servicenow-table-sync/3b215427-ef27-4ece-9d6c-d090047e71d4.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/servicenow-table-sync","prompt_id":"f7c939ca-0968-4d4a-8039-59a7188a4e60","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"UserPromptSubmit","prompt":"-\nYou are enhancing a Stonebranch UAC Universal Extension in the current workspace.\n\nAUTOMATION MODE — there is NO human available: never call AskUserQuestion; never spawn sub-agents or use the Agent/Task tool. Make all decisions autonomously and complete every edit without waiting for confirmation.\n\n## How to work\n\nThe working directory is the workspace root. All extension source lives under `extension-code/src/`.\n\n1. Read the extension source:\n   - `extension-code/src/extension.py` — action dispatch\n   - `extension-code/src/manager.py` — core logic (if present)\n   - `extension-code/src/actions/` — per-action modules\n   - `extension-code/src/fields/input.py` — field dataclasses\n   - `extension-code/src/templates/template.json` — field definitions and dynamic-choice config\n   - `extension-code/src/extension.yml` — name, version, api_level\n2. Learn the existing architecture, authentication, HTTP helpers, and output conventions before editing.\n3. Apply the enhancement by editing the relevant files with the Edit tool. Make only the changes needed — do not refactor unrelated code.\n4. Existing actions MUST keep working unchanged; existing tasks MUST NOT require any new required fields.\n\n## Enhancement Request\n\nEnhance and repair the existing Stonebranch Universal Extension that integrates with ServiceNow.\n\n## Problem\n\nDynamic-choice refreshes fail before any ServiceNow data is returned:\n\n* `Failure while refreshing choices for field \"Customer Table\". {Missing ServiceNow credential fields}`\n* `Failure while refreshing choices for field \"Target Fields\". {Missing ServiceNow credential fields}`\n* `Failure while refreshing choices for field \"Customer Record Override\". {Missing ServiceNow credential fields}`\n\nIn the refresh dialog:\n\n* An Agent is selected.\n* The generic Stonebranch `Credentials` field is blank.\n* The required custom `ServiceNow Credential` field contains a credential reference.\n* `ServiceNow Credential Variable` is unchecked.\n* No environment variables are shown.\n\nThe generic Credentials field is the Agent OS execution identity and must not be treated as the ServiceNow API credential.\n\n## Stonebranch contract to follow\n\nA Universal Template field of type `Credential` is delivered to the extension as a Python dictionary shaped like:\n\n```python\n{\n    \"user\": \"...\",\n    \"password\": \"...\",\n    \"keyLocation\": \"...\",\n    \"passphrase\": \"...\",\n    \"token\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\nFor Basic Authentication, use the exact keys `user` and `password`. Do not expect `username`, `runtimeUser`, `runtimePassword`, `credentialName`, `instance_url`, or `url` inside this dictionary.\n\nDynamic-choice methods receive only the fields configured as their dependent fields.\n\n## Required work\n\n1. Search the repository for the literal error message `Missing ServiceNow credential fields` and trace every path that creates it.\n\n2. Inspect all relevant files, including:\n\n   * `template.json` or other Universal Template definitions\n   * `extension.py`\n   * ServiceNow client/authentication modules\n   * Dynamic-choice decorators and handlers\n   * Tests, packaging metadata, and `extension.yml`\n\n3. Identify and document the exact root cause before modifying code. In particular, check for:\n\n   * Reading `username` instead of `user`\n   * Treating the credential value as a name/string instead of a dictionary\n   * Using the UI label instead of the template field’s internal Name\n   * Expecting the ServiceNow instance URL inside the credential\n   * A mismatch between the template field name and Python lookup key\n   * Missing dependent-field configuration\n   * An unresolvable credential or blank Runtime User/Runtime Password\n   * Different credential-handling logic between task launch and dynamic-choice execution\n\n4. Implement one centralized credential/connection resolver used by both normal task execution and every dynamic-choice handler. It must:\n\n   * Obtain the credential using the exact internal field name from the template.\n   * Validate that it is a dictionary.\n   * Read Basic Auth from `credential[\"user\"]` and `credential[\"password\"]`.\n   * Read `credential[\"token\"]` only if token authentication is already supported by the extension.\n   * Treat empty strings as missing.\n   * Never derive the ServiceNow hostname from the credential name.\n   * Never log credential values.\n   * Return clear, actionable validation errors naming missing configuration fields without exposing secrets.\n\n5. Ensure the ServiceNow instance/base URL is represented by a separate required text field, unless a correctly implemented equivalent already exists. Normalize it safely:\n\n   * Require `https://` unless the existing product requirements explicitly permit HTTP.\n   * Remove trailing slashes.\n   * Do not place the URL inside the credential object.\n   * Do not derive it from a username or credential name.\n\n6. Correct every dynamic-choice dependency definition:\n\n   * `Customer Table`: ServiceNow URL, ServiceNow Credential, and authentication type if applicable.\n   * `Target Fields`: all connection fields plus Customer Table.\n   * `Customer Record Override`: all connection fields plus Customer Table and any query/filter field it requires.\n\n   Use the actual internal template field names, not the displayed labels. Ensure each `@dynamic_choice_command(...)` value exactly matches the corresponding dynamic-choice field’s internal Name.\n\n7. If the connection URL or other required setting is supplied through environment variables, configure the template to send environment variables during Dynamic Choice operations. Prefer an explicit task field for the URL when that produces a clearer and more reliable interface.\n\n8. Improve error handling:\n\n   * Configuration error: identify the missing field or credential key.\n   * HTTP 401/403: report authentication/authorization failure.\n   * DNS, TLS, connection, and timeout errors: report connection failure.\n   * Other ServiceNow HTTP errors: include status code and a sanitized response summary.\n   * Return failures through the appropriate `ExtensionResult` rather than an unhandled exception.\n   * Never include passwords, tokens, authorization headers, or full credential dictionaries in logs or errors.\n\n9. Add safe diagnostic logging at debug level showing only:\n\n   * Dynamic-choice handler name\n   * Top-level field names received\n   * Credential dictionary key names\n   * Value types\n   * Sanitized ServiceNow hostname\n\n10. Add or update automated tests covering:\n\n* Basic Auth credential: `{\"user\": \"svc-user\", \"password\": \"secret\"}`\n* Token credential when supported\n* Missing credential field\n* Credential supplied as the wrong type\n* Missing `user`\n* Missing `password`\n* Missing ServiceNow URL\n* Dynamic-choice input containing only configured dependent fields\n* All three affected dynamic choices\n* No secret values appearing in logs or error messages\n* Successful creation of the same ServiceNow client during launch and dynamic-choice execution\n\n11. Run the full test suite and the UIP validation/build commands supported by this repository. Resolve all failures introduced by the change.\n\n12. Increment the extension patch version and add a changelog entry describing the credential-resolution and dynamic-choice dependency fix.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n* Selecting a valid Resolvable Stonebranch credential with Runtime User and Runtime Password successfully refreshes Customer Table.\n* Selecting a Customer Table successfully refreshes Target Fields.\n* Customer Record Override refreshes without credential-field errors.\n* Normal task execution and dynamic choices use the same connection-resolution code.\n* Leaving the generic Agent `Credentials` field blank remains supported unless the Agent itself requires an OS identity.\n* Missing configuration produces a specific message, such as:\n\n  * `ServiceNow Credential is required`\n  * `ServiceNow Credential must be a resolved Credential object`\n  * `ServiceNow Credential is missing Runtime User`\n  * `ServiceNow Credential is missing Runtime Password`\n  * `ServiceNow Instance URL is required`\n* No password or token is exposed anywhere.\n\nAt completion, provide:\n\n1. The confirmed root cause, with filenames and line references.\n2. A concise summary of changes.\n3. Tests and validation commands executed, with results.\n4. Any required UAC template migration or re-import instructions.\n5. Exact steps to verify all three dynamic-choice fields in Universal Controller.\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n1. **showIfField / requireIfField** in template.json: the value must be the `fieldMapping` value (e.g. \"Choice Field 1\"), NOT the field's `name`.\n2. **showIfFieldValue / requireIfFieldValue**: set the exact value to match on, or `null` to show for ANY non-empty value. Always include the key explicitly — never omit it.\n3. **variablePrefix** in template.json must stay as the existing value; scripts read fields as `${ops_<prefix>_<fieldname>}` substituted at runtime, not via os.environ.\n4. **Required top-level template.json fields** must remain present: minReleaseLevel, exportReleaseLevel, sendEnvironment, sendVariables, agentFieldsRestriction, credentialFieldsRestriction.\n5. **fieldType**: use \"Plain\" for multi-line text, never \"Large Text\" (UAC rejects it).\n6. **sysId**: every field entry needs a globally unique 32-char hex sysId (no dashes). Generate a fresh unique sysId for each new field.\n7. **Dynamic choice fields**: in template.json set `\"choiceDynamic\": true`, `\"choices\": []`, and `\"choiceFields\": [...]` (fieldMapping values passed as context); in the action module add a method decorated with `@dynamic_choice_command(\"field_name\")` (matching the field's `name`) returning `[{\"name\": \"Label\", \"value\": \"value\"}, ...]`.\n8. Edit files directly — do not invoke skills or spawn agents.\n\nAfter all edits, print a one-line summary of what changed.\n"}

